    {
      "id": "claim_ea1c5cf15bac4c18b59e13029e4d86b1",
      "statement": "sendOutOfRangeNotifications schedules a single coalesced local notification for the whole alert batch (title carries the count) on the Android channel 'out-of-range' at HIGH importance, with a 1-second TIME_INTERVAL trigger and tap data { screen: 'positions' }; despite the doc comment's 'one local notification per alert', the implementation always emits one notification, and the whole body is wrapped in a try/catch that logs and swallows failures so a notification error never propagates to its caller.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/utils/alerts/outOfRange.ts#L48-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f59f8790002556090453ebd0d91d8f5262d182ef28192ab9cf51363fe16f1d6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0aec6a5871e84d498000b99b65489b11",
      "statement": "alertStore owns a dedicated MMKV instance created with createMMKV({ id: 'alerts' }) and stores all state under a single key out_of_range_state: one JSON record mapping wallet address to RangeStateMap (position id -> inRange boolean from the last background check). getRangeState returns null for an unseen wallet or on unparseable JSON; clearRangeState deletes only that wallet's entry and wipes the whole key if the record cannot be parsed, so corrupt storage never poisons a later comparison.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/stores/alertStore.ts#L1-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c8773134305d64109f1f9debffd944f9ac2854bfb29d8178aae72193ef269daa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a326298114fa4628897a77d5b24390a6",
      "statement": "Unlike its siblings, setRangeState does not guard its JSON.parse: a corrupt stored record makes it throw, which lands in the background task's alert try/catch (logged as 'widgetBackgroundSync: alert check failed' and swallowed) rather than crashing the task.",
