    {
      "id": "claim_212e1ae81d4346fdabbab82070ed02fa",
      "statement": "The entire alert block (setting read, portfolio load, store reads/writes, send) runs inside its own try/catch, and sendOutOfRangeNotifications swallows its own errors; the task's BackgroundFetchResult therefore reflects only the widget sync outcome — NewData for 'updated', NoData for 'no-data', Failed only when syncWidgets throws or returns 'failed' — so notification or RPC failures can never get the task throttled by the OS.",
